  "instruction": "Claude r20 (2026-09-28): 「몇 번 갔나 · 남은 이벤트」 where the player picks people (design ingame/설계_v3_글메뉴판.md 「r20 요구」). Codex must never run publish_calendar_*.py --restore or otherwise remove the calendar overlay (KR_T9*/KR_T17*/KR_T18*/KR_T19*/KR_T20* functions, the nine r15 same-length operands, the RunEvent operand swap in KR_T9HomeCasual, the seven r20 same-length operands in C_Status::RunStatus, C_HomeStatusView@SetInfo, C_SceneTraining@RunSelectPartner and C_SceneTraining@_UpdateInputPartner). The calendar is a permanent user-requested feature: when a rebuild needs a clean base, rebase on the runtime that current.json points to and carry the calendar functions forward; restore is reserved for the user's explicit request. Payload: NightRemaster.ain only; PACT/EX/FNL and the help-menu chart untouched. KR_T20* functions appended; no original function relocated, no forwarder, no new global / struct member / session variable, no save schema change. Seven same-length operand swaps (a method call is PUSH <function> ... CALLMETHOD n, so its target is the PUSH operand): C_Status::RunStatus PrevPage -> KR_T20StPrev, NextPage -> KR_T20StNext, AFL_Parts_EraseWholeMouseWheelEvent -> KR_T20StEnd; C_HomeStatusView@SetInfo SetActivePage -> KR_T20StActive; C_SceneTraining@RunSelectPartner C_SceneTrainingView@SelectAlly::get (the direction-key loop) -> KR_T20TrAlly and ■方向キー処理／削除 -> KR_T20TrKeyDel; C_SceneTraining@_UpdateInputPartner AppearStandChara -> KR_T20TrAppear. Effects: the status window pages cycle 1-2-3-4 (4 = 「이벤트」: 특훈 뒤 대화 n번 봄, 이달 남은 특훈 뒤 대화 m, 던전 동행 남은 장면 per partner, drawn as two runtime parts 2026092001/2026092002 under the status activity root and released when the page or the window closes); the Saturday partner selection shows a box + two-line label (parts 2026092020+p / 2026092010+p under each shown portrait, hovered person bright) released after every wait (so never in a save, the confirm dialog or the save/load screens). Counts come only from IsRegisteredEvent of this save and the calendar tables: C_Ability.training is a point pool (not a count) and the game keeps no per-person dungeon companion count. Pinned (index, address and every code byte identical): KR_T9HomeCasual, KR_T9HomeConfig, C_SceneHomebase@CheckGameSysButtons, C_SceneHomebase@Run, LSys3xScript::RunEvent, KR_T18RunSandboxed. r19's five and r18's eight forwarders and r15's nine / r18's one same-length sites stay. Every earlier contract stays in force.",
